# Deployment record — TEMPLATE

Copy to `deployment.local.md` (sibling of this file) and fill in. That filename
is **gitignored**: this repo is open source and multi-tenant, so hostnames,
addresses, stack ids and account numbers must not be committed. They are both an
unnecessary disclosure and values that stop being true for anyone else.

Keep this current. The point of recording it at all is so a future reader can
tell configuration from aspiration — "this is what is actually running" is a
different claim from "this is what the config would do".

**Never put secrets here.** Tokens and passwords belong in `/etc/default/alloy`
on the host (mode `0600`). Record the *name* of an access policy token and what
it is scoped to, never its value. This file is gitignored, not encrypted — a
copied working tree or a stray `git add -f` still exposes it.

---

## Hosts

| | |
|---|---|
| Purpose | e.g. agent-server / app + storage |
| Address | |
| Hostname | |
| `instance` label | set explicitly; do not leave it to the hostname |
| Config path | `/etc/alloy/config.alloy` |
| Synced by | deploy workflow, or "by hand — drift risk" |
| Repo config | `apps/agent-server/observability/` or `observability/coolify-host/` |

Duplicate the block per host.

## Which host serves production

Record the evidence, not the assumption — a running control-plane stack is not
the same as one that has deployed anything. For Coolify:

```sh
docker exec coolify-db psql -U coolify -d coolify \
  -c 'select count(*) from applications' \
  -c 'select count(*) from application_deployment_queues' \
  -c 'select id, name, ip from servers'
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/http/routers
```

| Host | applications | deployments | Traefik routers | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|

## Database

Which database actually serves production, and therefore whether the compose
`postgres` service is real or vestigial. This decides whether a
`postgres_exporter` belongs in the Alloy config — see the note in
`observability/coolify-host/alloy.alloy`.

## Observability backend

| | |
|---|---|
| Alloy version | |
| Grafana Cloud org / stack / region | |
| Loki endpoint + numeric username | |
| Prometheus endpoint + numeric username | |
| Access policy token name(s) and scopes | **names only, never values** |
| Dashboards installed | |

The Loki and Prometheus usernames are **different numbers**. Record both, and
check them against each other before first push — swapping them yields a 401
that reads exactly like a bad token.

## Series budget

Grafana Cloud's free tier allows 10k active series across all hosts. Measured
per host, so a collector change can be checked against a real number rather than
an estimate:

```sh
curl -s localhost:12345/metrics | grep prometheus_remote_storage_samples_in_total
ip -o link | wc -l   # a Docker host's interface count drives most of the cost
```

| Host | samples/scrape | notes |
|---|---|---|

## Open gaps

Things known to be unmonitored or known-broken, with the remediation and why it
has not been done. A gap that is written down is a decision; one that is not is
an accident waiting to be discovered mid-incident.
